<h2>Our Residential Claim Process</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Free claim review.</strong> We talk through what happened, what the insurer has said so far, and whether representation makes sense.</li>
<li><strong>Policy review.</strong> We read your declarations page, coverages, endorsements, and exclusions.</li>
<li><strong>Inspection and documentation.</strong> We inspect the roof, exterior, interior, and other structures, and document with photos and Matterport 3D imaging where it helps.</li>
<li><strong>Estimate.</strong> We prepare a detailed Xactimate estimate reflecting the full scope and local pricing.</li>
<li><strong>Presentation and negotiation.</strong> We submit the claim package and handle communication with the insurer’s adjuster.</li>
<li><strong>Supplements and follow-through.</strong> If more damage is found during repairs, we help document a <a href="/services/insurance-claim-supplements/">supplement</a> and track recoverable depreciation.</li>
</ol>

<h2>When a Homeowner Should Consider Help</h2>
<ul>
<li>The damage is extensive, hidden, or spread across multiple parts of the home.</li>
<li>The settlement offer does not cover your contractor’s repair cost.</li>
<li>The claim is delayed, partially denied, or the insurer keeps asking for more information.</li>
<li>You feel overwhelmed by the paperwork while also managing repairs and family life.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What We Do Not Do</h2>
<p>A public adjuster represents the insured only. We do not perform repairs on a claim we adjust, and we do not give legal advice. If your claim involves a lawsuit, bad faith, or a deadline to sue, we recommend speaking with a Texas attorney. We also cannot promise a particular settlement. Our job is to make sure the claim is accurate, well documented, and clearly presented.</p>
<p>Fees are disclosed in a written contract before any work begins; Texas law caps public adjuster compensation at 10% of the insurance settlement. To find out whether we can help with your homeowners claim, request a <a href="/free-claim-review/">Free Claim Review</a>.</p>
